  annotation "note_1771576703371_1", anchor: "the unit had already been formally dissolved", text: "Formally dissolved. Performing unauthorized operations. At an Aurora site. During the Orca Incursion. With enough coordination to execute Grulkzul Omega Strike from a trade-platform — a casting requiring, at minimum, three practitioners in synchronized position. The Nightshelf's genius for institutional fiction has always been their ability to disband a unit and deploy it simultaneously without apparent contradiction. The paperwork dissolving the Midnight Claws and the operational orders sending them to the Dawn Terrace are filed in adjacent strata. One admires the filing system, if nothing else.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576703371_2", anchor: "seventeen confirmed dead", text: "Seventeen. A prime number in a casualty report. I am so conditioned by round-number inflation that an odd, indivisible figure strikes me as practically a primary source. Someone counted these.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576703371_3", anchor: "a shrine to something that was not the aurora", text: "The ice preserves the dedication marks clearly enough to identify the recipient. I chose not to name it in the main text because the E'frostlings' surviving leadership have been cooperative with my requests for access to their administrative strata, and I would like them to remain so. Draw your own conclusions from the volcanic stone.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576703371_4", anchor: "The rhymes count to eighteen", text: "I have now documented children's counting games producing more accurate site intelligence than official surveys at three separate locations. The Forgotten Shore. Nightfall Shelf. Here. Fledglings absorb what adults won't say and preserve it in meter. If this edition survives 'the transition,' some future archivist will find the most reliable corruption cartography on The Berg encoded in nursery rhymes. One hopes they find that as entertaining as I do.", type: :commentary, display: :full
